      "body": "## Motivation\n\nPaged SWA decode allocates from the full-attention and sliding-window pools sequentially. If either pool is exhausted, the other allocation can consume a page before the composite returns `None`, stranding unmapped KV capacity. Repeated rejected decodes can drain the healthy pool.\n\n## Modifications\n\nCheck the exact decode page demand against both pools before either allocation. Preserve partial-page reuse and the full-only per-request ring path.\n\nAdd a CPU regression using real paged allocator bookkeeping and GPU regressions covering both exhaustion directions, retry after freeing a page, staged releases, and decoding with no free pages.\n\nRelated #30892 and #34400 change the individual paged allocator's kernel admission; this fixes the separate composite allocation leak.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThe CPU regression fails on main in both exhaustion directions because the healthy pool's free-page list changes.\n\nPassed locally:\n```bash\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=99 PYTHONPATH=python .venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s test/registered/unit/mem_cache -p 'test_swa*page*.py' -q\n# 13 tests passed\n\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 PYTHONPATH=python .venv/bin/python test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_swa_unittest.py -q\n# 26 tests passed on NVIDIA A30, including real allocation kernels\n```\n\nNo model forward or sampling changes. NPU/ROCm hardware was not exercised.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo serving throughput benchmark or performance claim. Admission uses the existing CPU sequence-length mirror and adds no GPU synchronization.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code with pre-commit.\n- [x] Add CI-registered regression tests.\n- [x] Follow SGLang code style.\n- Documentation: no public API/configuration change.\n- Accuracy/speed model benchmarks: not run; allocator correctness results are above.\n\nAI assistance: Codex assisted with the implementation, regression tests, and PR description.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37124913940](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37124913940)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37124913837](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37124913837)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37124913910](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37124913910)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
